course: dictionary
lesson: 15523
title: Substitution: one thing in place of another
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A substitution is putting one person or thing in the place of another. The word comes from substitute, which also means a replacement. When you meet substitution in a text, look for the word «in place of» or «instead» nearby, because those clues often show what is being swapped.
explain: In sport, the coach makes a substitution: «The coach made a substitution, so a tired player came off and a fresh one went on.» The new player takes the old player's place for the rest of the match.
explain: In maths, substitution means putting a number in place of a letter. «If a = 3, find 2a + 1.» Substitute 3 for a: 2 × 3 + 1 = 7. The value of the expression is 7.
explain: Cooks make substitutions too. «Ella had no butter, so she used oil instead.» Oil is a substitution for butter. Always check that the swap still makes sense, just as you do when you swap a word into a sentence.
fact: Substitution means putting one person or thing in the place of another.
fact: In sport, a substitution is when a player is taken off and another player comes on.
fact: In maths, substitution means replacing a letter in an expression or formula with a number to find its value.
fact: In cooking, a substitution is using a different ingredient instead of the one in the recipe.
fact: In a substitution cipher, each letter is swapped for another letter, so A might become D.
exercise: «The coach made a substitution in the second half.» What is a substitution in a football match? | A rule about the weather | A goal scored by the team | A training session before the match | *A player taken off and replaced by another player
exercise: Mia has 2x + 1 and x = 5. She puts 5 in place of x. What is this step called? | Rounding | *Substitution | Division | Addition
exercise: «Ella had no butter, so she used oil instead.» What does the oil show? | *A substitution for the butter | A mistake that cannot be fixed | A kind of cake | A new recipe book
test: Which word means putting one thing in the place of another? | Decoration | *Substitution | Subtraction | Multiplication
test: «If a = 3, find 2a + 1.» What number do you put in place of a? | 2 | 7 | *3 | 1
exam: In a substitution cipher, A becomes D and B becomes E. What does the code do? | It puts the letters in alphabetical order | It adds numbers to each letter | *It swaps each letter for another letter | It deletes every second letter
